<%# HOME PAGE OFFERS. Three boxes, one per offer, each with one button to its
    own page (Tom's decision of 21/10/2026, "DECISION AND PLAN - Simplify to
    three offers"). Rendered inside the home page hero, under the headline, in
    place of the hero's own button, so the page opens with one headline and
    three boxes. The copy, prices and links come from lib/mainNav.js
    (homeOffers), where every line is already approved on the page it leads
    to. Styles are in views/index.ejs (.home-offers), the only view that
    renders this. Expects: homeOffers. Followed by one line that points at
    the enquiry form. %>
<div class="home-offers" data-home-offers>
    <% homeOffers.forEach(function (o) { %>
    <div class="home-offer" data-offer="<%= o.id %>">
        <p class="home-offer-audience"><%= o.audience %></p>
        <h2 class="home-offer-name"><%= o.name %></h2>
        <p class="home-offer-price"><%= o.price %></p>
        <p class="home-offer-line"><%= o.line %></p>
        <a href="<%= o.href %>" class="btn btn-primary home-offer-btn"><%= o.button %></a>
    </div>
    <% }); %>
</div>
<%# One line under the boxes (Tom's yes of 21/10/2026): the first
    conversation is free, linking to the enquiry form in the footer. The
    second sentence is the same sentence the form itself carries
    (site-footer.ejs, .lead-form-next), so the boxes never say something the
    form does not. %>
<p class="home-offers-note" data-home-offers-note>Not sure which is right for you? <a href="#conversation">The first conversation is free and there's no obligation.</a></p>
